  </Preview>

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUDITH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ROBERT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>SCENE 1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Notations">
      <Text>DR. JUDITH BROWNE’s consulting room in a New York Health Center. There is a main door to the reception area of the practice and a back door. It is a post-war building, with Victorian trimmings around the main door and the frames. This play goes further in describing the setting.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Notations">
      <Text>This format uses Times New Roman font.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Notations">
      <Text>Notice that the opening description uses the Notations element in this form.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Notations">
      <Text>Stage action not reliant on dialogue, however, uses an Action element and is formatted as below.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Notations">
      <Text>This is one type of format for dramatic stage play. You can modify the elements any way you want by going to Format &gt; Elements.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A SILENCE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JUDITH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I have something to tell you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ROBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JUDITH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I love you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>ROBERT takes a breath to speak but JUDITH stops him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ROBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Judith.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JUDITH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh, what you must think?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ROBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Come on, now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JUDITH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s true. I can’t help it. I know you should never become involved with a patient.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ROBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Judith, I love you too.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She looks at him her mouth open a little. For a moment she is lost.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A SILENCE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Then she allows ROBERT to help her back onto the chair. She smoothes her clothes down. ROBERT returns to his chair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JUDITH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I-I can’t believe it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ROBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s true.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The lost look is on JUDITH’s face again. ROBERT speaks very gently.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You heard what you wanted to hear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A PAUSE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>And JUDITH is near tears.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>FADE TO BLACK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

